# Sample Excel File Template
# Rename this file to sample_reels.xlsx and add real Instagram URLs

To create your Excel file:

1. Create a new Excel spreadsheet
2. Add the following columns:

   | Instagram URL | Reel Title | Notes |
   |--------------|------------|-------|
   | https://www.instagram.com/reel/YOUR_SHORTCODE/ | My First Reel | Optional notes |
   | https://www.instagram.com/reel/YOUR_SHORTCODE/ | My Second Reel | Optional notes |

3. Save as .xlsx format

Column Requirements:
- "Instagram URL" column is required (must contain valid Instagram reel URLs)
- Other columns are optional but will be preserved
- The application will add a "Transcription" column with results

URL Format Examples:
- https://www.instagram.com/reel/ABC123/
- https://instagram.com/reel/ABC123/
- https://www.instagram.com/p/ABC123/

Important Notes:
- Make sure URLs are complete and valid
- Only public reels can be downloaded without login
- For private content, enable Instagram login in the app
- Test with 2-3 reels first before processing large batches
